# The region set this deployment actually builds. Read by scripts/graphhopper.sh
# under GH_REGION_SET=custom; one "geofabrik/path|minlon,minlat,maxlon,maxlat"
# per line, an empty bbox meaning take the whole extract, '#' comments stripped.
#
# ⚠ ALL THREE LINES ARE REQUIRED. `regions_for_set()` is a plain case statement:
# `custom` REPLACES the set, it does not extend `demo`. A file holding only the
# Sri Lanka line silently drops Greater London and Noord-Holland, which takes out
# three of the five TEST_LOCATIONS, all three of verify_selfhosted.py's in-graph
# assertions, and the London origin the layout gate drives the app from.

# Sri Lanka entire. The demo set cut this to a 1x1 degree box around Colombo,
# which put Ella (6.875 N, 81.038 E) 76 km outside the eastern edge and told a
# Sri Lankan user that Meander does not cover their country. Measured before the
# change, straight off the running router: bbox
# [-1.449894, 6.379104, 80.389202, 54.991951], which Coverage.describe() renders
# as "roughly 6°N to 55°N, 1°W to 80°E" — the exact sentence in the report.
#
# 143.7 MB of extract (already on disk and verified, dated 2026-08-09) against
# the 45.7 MB cut. It brings in Kandy, Galle, Nuwara Eliya, Jaffna and
# Trincomalee as well, and Ella at 1,041 m is the first test location that is
# not at sea level.
asia/sri-lanka|

# Unchanged from the demo set. See the note above about why they are here.
europe/united-kingdom/england/greater-london|-0.65,51.02,0.36,52.03
europe/netherlands/noord-holland|4.36,51.86,5.37,52.86
